# Three Components

A border requires three values:
- **width** (e.g., `2px`, `medium`)
- **style** (required – `solid`, `dotted`, `dashed`, `double`, `none`)
- **color** (keyword, hex, etc.)

Shorthand: `border: 2px solid red;`

You can target each side: `border-left`, `border-right`, `border-top`, `border-bottom`. Even finer: `border-top-style`, etc.

```css
.card {
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  border-radius: 8px;
}
```

slides.codeSnippet:
.solid  { border: 3px solid black; }
.dotted { border: 3px dotted teal; }
.dashed { border: 3px dashed orange; }
.double { border: 5px double purple; }
.groove { border: 5px groove gray; }

.avatar {
  width: 80px;
  height: 80px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  overflow: hidden; /* if image spills */
}

slides.content:
# The `outline` Property

`outline` is similar to border but:
- Does not take up space (drawn outside the element, on top of surrounding content).
- Used primarily for focus indicators (a11y).
- Can be offset with `outline-offset`.

```css
input:focus {
  outline: 2px solid blue;
  outline-offset: 2px;
}
```
Outline is not part of the box model; it doesn't affect layout.
